WEBVTT

00:00:00.102 --> 00:00:05.822
When we create categories exact boundaries need to
be intentional Here

00:00:05.848 --> 00:00:11.163
our billing rule begins with missing values Then we
handle amounts greater

00:00:11.188 --> 00:00:15.571
than or equal to ten thousand Next we handle amounts
greater than

00:00:15.597 --> 00:00:20.662
or equal to five thousand Everything else goes into
the low-value category

00:00:21.576 --> 00:00:25.030
If we add a special zero category zero also needs to
appear

00:00:25.043 --> 00:00:28.973
before the broad final ELSE branch When you design a
rule like

00:00:28.999 --> 00:00:34.760
this test the exact boundary values Try zero five
thousand ten thousand

00:00:35.017 --> 00:00:39.115
a value just below each threshold and a null value A
query

00:00:39.141 --> 00:00:42.479
that works for ordinary records may still contain a
logic error at

00:00:42.504 --> 00:00:46.680
the boundaries so boundary testing is an important
part of validating SQL
